 156 156 92-93 2 0 0 250-250 0 0-2 93-92-156-156-156 156 94 92 0 2-250 0 0-250 0 0 93 93 157-156-157-156-93 94 0 0 0-250 250 0 0 0-94 93 156 157 156-157-93-93 0 0 250 0 0 250z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div><div class="modebar-group"><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Show closest data on hover" data-attr="hovermode" data-val="closest" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="ne"><svg viewBox="0 0 1500 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m375 725l0 0-375-375 375-374 0-1 1125 0 0 750-1125 0z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn active" data-title="Compare data on hover" data-attr="hovermode" data-val="x" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="ne"><svg viewBox="0 0 1125 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m187 786l0 2-187-188 188-187 0 0 937 0 0 373-938 0z m0-499l0 1-187-188 188-188 0 0 937 0 0 376-938-1z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div></div></div><svg class="main-svg" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" width="646.6666666666667" height="365"><g class="hoverlayer"></g></svg></div></div></div></foreignObject></g><text class="draggable" name="text" x="357" y="151" r="0" rtemp="0" transform="rotate(0 357 151)" style="fill: rgb(255, 0, 89); font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-size: 15px; font-family: bold;">out1</text><g transform="translate(477,25)" x="477" y="25" title="codeHTML" width="502" height="734" class="codeHTML" name="codeHTML" rot="0"><foreignObject x="0" y="0" width="222" height="200" style="height: 734px; width: 836.667px;"><div name="htmlCode" style="zoom: 60%; height: 734px; width: 836.667px;" code="<div class=&quot;ch&quot;>
    
    <h1>Triangle Wave Generator (Astable + Integrator) - SPICE Time Domain Analysis</h1>

    <div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;>
        <h2>Circuit Components</h2>
        <h3 style=&quot;color: #2980b9;&quot;>Stage 1: Astable Multivibrator (Square Wave Generator)</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Op-Amp 1:</strong> TL084</li>
            <li><strong>R1:</strong> 1 kΩ (feedback resistor)</li>
            <li><strong>R2, R3:</strong> 1 kΩ each (hysteresis network)</li>
            <li><strong>C1:</strong> 1 μF (timing capacitor)</li>
            <li><strong>V1, V2:</strong> ±10V power supply</li>
            <li><strong>Output:</strong> V(out1) - Square wave</li>
        </ul>
        <h3 style=&quot;color: #c0392b; margin-top: 15px;&quot;>Stage 2: Integrator (Triangle Wave Generator)</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Op-Amp 2:</strong> TL084</li>
            <li><strong>R6:</strong> 1 kΩ (input resistor)</li>
            <li><strong>C2:</strong> 0.7 μF (integrating capacitor)</li>
            <li><strong>R4:</strong> 100 kΩ (DC feedback - prevents saturation)</li>
            <li><strong>R5:</strong> 1 kΩ (bias compensation)</li>
            <li><strong>V3, V4:</strong> ±10V power supply</li>
            <li><strong>Output:</strong> V(out2) - Triangle wave</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Oscillation Frequency</h2>
    <div class=&quot;ch-formula&quot;>
        Stage 1 (Astable):<br>
        β = R3/(R2+R3) = 0.5, Thresholds = ±5V<br>
        T₁ = 2·R1·C1·ln((1+β)/(1-β)) = 2·1k·1μF·ln(3) ≈ 2.2 ms<br>
        f ≈ <strong>455 Hz</strong><br><br>
        Stage 2 (Integrator):<br>
        Vout2 = -(1/R6·C2) ∫ Vout1 dt<br>
        Triangle amplitude = (Vsquare · T) / (4·R6·C2)
    </div>

    <h2>Simulation Results</h2>
    <div class=&quot;ch-grid&quot;>

        <div class=&quot;ch-col blue&quot;>
            <h3>Square Wave V(out1) - Red</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Generated by the astable multivibrator (Stage 1)</li>
                <li>Amplitude: approximately ±8V</li>
                <li>Frequency: ~455 Hz (period ≈ 2.2 ms)</li>
                <li>50% duty cycle (symmetric)</li>
                <li>Feeds into the integrator stage</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class=&quot;ch-col red&quot;>
            <h3>Triangle Wave V(out2) - Blue</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Generated by the integrator (Stage 2)</li>
                <li>Amplitude: approximately ±5V</li>
                <li>Same frequency as square wave (~455 Hz)</li>
                <li>Linear rising and falling slopes</li>
                <li>90° phase relationship with square wave</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

    </div>

    <div class=&quot;ch-card green-border&quot;>
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p style=&quot;line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;&quot;>This circuit is a <strong>Triangle Wave Generator</strong> composed of two cascaded stages. The first stage is an <strong>astable multivibrator</strong> that produces a square wave by alternately charging and discharging capacitor C1 through the hysteresis network (R2, R3). The second stage is an <strong>integrator</strong> that converts the square wave into a triangle wave by integrating the constant positive and negative voltage levels of the square wave, producing linear ramps. The resistor R4 (100 kΩ) provides DC feedback to prevent the integrator from saturating due to op-amp offset voltage. The result is two synchronized outputs: a square wave and a triangle wave at the same frequency (~455 Hz).</p>
    </div>

    <div class=&quot;ch-card&quot; style=&quot;background-color: #e8f8f5; border-left: 4px solid #1abc9c;&quot;>
        <h2 style=&quot;color: #16a085;&quot;>Circuit Operation Details</h2>
        <ul style=&quot;line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;&quot;>
            <li><strong>Square → Triangle:</strong> Integration of constant voltage produces linear ramp</li>
            <li><strong>Positive square input:</strong> Capacitor C2 charges linearly → negative ramp</li>
            <li><strong>Negative square input:</strong> Capacitor C2 discharges linearly → positive ramp</li>
            <li><strong>R4 role:</strong> Prevents DC drift and integrator saturation</li>
            <li><strong>Applications:</strong> Function generators, PWM generation, audio synthesizers, test equipment</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

</div>"><div class="ch">
    
    <h1>Triangle Wave Generator (Astable + Integrator) - SPICE Time Domain Analysis</h1>

    <div class="ch-card">
        <h2>Circuit Components</h2>
        <h3 style="color: #2980b9;">Stage 1: Astable Multivibrator (Square Wave Generator)</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Op-Amp 1:</strong> TL084</li>
            <li><strong>R1:</strong> 1 kΩ (feedback resistor)</li>
            <li><strong>R2, R3:</strong> 1 kΩ each (hysteresis network)</li>
            <li><strong>C1:</strong> 1 μF (timing capacitor)</li>
            <li><strong>V1, V2:</strong> ±10V power supply</li>
            <li><strong>Output:</strong> V(out1) - Square wave</li>
        </ul>
        <h3 style="color: #c0392b; margin-top: 15px;">Stage 2: Integrator (Triangle Wave Generator)</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Op-Amp 2:</strong> TL084</li>
            <li><strong>R6:</strong> 1 kΩ (input resistor)</li>
            <li><strong>C2:</strong> 0.7 μF (integrating capacitor)</li>
            <li><strong>R4:</strong> 100 kΩ (DC feedback - prevents saturation)</li>
            <li><strong>R5:</strong> 1 kΩ (bias compensation)</li>
            <li><strong>V3, V4:</strong> ±10V power supply</li>
            <li><strong>Output:</strong> V(out2) - Triangle wave</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Oscillation Frequency</h2>
    <div class="ch-formula">
        Stage 1 (Astable):<br>
        β = R3/(R2+R3) = 0.5, Thresholds = ±5V<br>
        T₁ = 2·R1·C1·ln((1+β)/(1-β)) = 2·1k·1μF·ln(3) ≈ 2.2 ms<br>
        f ≈ <strong>455 Hz</strong><br><br>
        Stage 2 (Integrator):<br>
        Vout2 = -(1/R6·C2) ∫ Vout1 dt<br>
        Triangle amplitude = (Vsquare · T) / (4·R6·C2)
    </div>

    <h2>Simulation Results</h2>
    <div class="ch-grid">

        <div class="ch-col blue">
            <h3>Square Wave V(out1) - Red</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Generated by the astable multivibrator (Stage 1)</li>
                <li>Amplitude: approximately ±8V</li>
                <li>Frequency: ~455 Hz (period ≈ 2.2 ms)</li>
                <li>50% duty cycle (symmetric)</li>
                <li>Feeds into the integrator stage</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="ch-col red">
            <h3>Triangle Wave V(out2) - Blue</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Generated by the integrator (Stage 2)</li>
                <li>Amplitude: approximately ±5V</li>
                <li>Same frequency as square wave (~455 Hz)</li>
                <li>Linear rising and falling slopes</li>
                <li>90° phase relationship with square wave</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

    </div>

    <div class="ch-card green-border">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">This circuit is a <strong>Triangle Wave Generator</strong> composed of two cascaded stages. The first stage is an <strong>astable multivibrator</strong> that produces a square wave by alternately charging and discharging capacitor C1 through the hysteresis network (R2, R3). The second stage is an <strong>integrator</strong> that converts the square wave into a triangle wave by integrating the constant positive and negative voltage levels of the square wave, producing linear ramps. The resistor R4 (100 kΩ) provides DC feedback to prevent the integrator from saturating due to op-amp offset voltage. The result is two synchronized outputs: a square wave and a triangle wave at the same frequency (~455 Hz).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ch-card" style="background-color: #e8f8f5; border-left: 4px solid #1abc9c;">
        <h2 style="color: #16a085;">Circuit Operation Details</h2>
        <ul style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
            <li><strong>Square → Triangle:</strong> Integration of constant voltage produces linear ramp</li>
            <li><strong>Positive square input:</strong> Capacitor C2 charges linearly → negative ramp</li>
            <li><strong>Negative square input:</strong> Capacitor C2 discharges linearly → positive ramp</li>
            <li><strong>R4 role:</strong> Prevents DC drift and integrator saturation</li>
            <li><strong>Applications:</strong> Function generators, PWM generation, audio synthesizers, test equipment</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

</div></div></foreignObject></g><g x="180" y="165" transform="translate(180,165)" width="25" height="35" class="part" name="part" xo="0" yo="0" sref="C1" directory="Basic" liblocale="true" symbolfile="Capacitor" model="Capacitor"><g width="200" top="40" left="0" height="200" version="0.0.1" zoom="10.399999999999993" reference="C" description="{&quot;webPage&quot;:&quot;https://pyams.sf.net/doc/Elements/Basic/Capacitor.html&quot;,&quot;info&quot;:&quot;&quot;}" symbolname="Capacitor" symbol="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Capacitor&quot;,&quot;reference&quot;:&quot;C&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Capacitor&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;std&quot;,&quot;std&quot;:{&quot;device&quot;:&quot;Capacitor&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;lib&quot;:{&quot;file&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;model&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;model&quot;:null}" device="std" type="null" model="Capacitor" modelname="Capacitor" modeltype="SPICE" destination="local"></g><g points="10,5 10,15" class="polyline" name="pin" type="simple" netid="7" netidpos="2" netId="7" netIdPos="2"><polyline points="10,5 10,15 " style="stroke: rgb(255, 0, 0); stroke-width: 1px;"></polyline><rect width="6" height="6" class="pin" x="7" y="2" style="stroke: rgb(0, 255, 0); fill: none; stroke-width: 1px; display: none;"></rect><text r="0" x="8" y="17" transform="rotate(90 8 17)" style="font-size: 12px; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; display: none; fill: rgb(0, 0, 0);">p</text><text r="0" x="10" y="5" transform="rotate(0 10 5)" style="font-size: 12px; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; display: none;">+</text><ellipse cx="10" cy="13.5" rx="1.5" ry="1.5" style="stroke: rgb(255, 0, 0); fill: rgb(255, 0, 0); stroke-width: 1px; display: none;"></ellipse><polygon points="8.5,15 11.5,15 10,16.5 " style="stroke: rgb(255, 0, 0); fill: rgb(255, 0, 0); stroke-width: 1px; display: none;"></polygon></g><g points="10,35 10,25" class="polyline" name="pin" type="simple" netid="10" netidpos="2" netId="10" netIdPos="2"><p